ChangeLog :
===========

2026/08/09 : 1.2.21

    Added the SPOP regression tests, in which the spop-client.py client speaks
    the protocol on its own and the spop-test.sh script starts the program for
    every test case and checks what it answers.  The new '--enable-sanitizer'
    configure option lets the tests detect the memory faults.

    Fixed the heap overflow that the second fragment of a frame caused, several
    defects in the memory allocation of the program and of the example agent,
    the handover of a new client to a busy worker, the release of the cURL data
    when a worker stops, the build without the cURL library, and the checks in
    several error paths.

    The connection backlog value is checked and the random generator is seeded
    at the program start now.  The string helpers moved to a shared source file,
    and the functions and the structures got their descriptions.

    - DOC: added the function and the structure descriptions
    - BUILD/MINOR: added the '--enable-sanitizer' configure option
    - MINOR: test: added the SPOP regression tests
    - BUG/MEDIUM: fixed the heap overflow when a frame was fragmented
    - BUG/MINOR: corrected the checks in several error paths
    - MINOR: checked the connection backlog and seeded the generator
    - BUILD/MINOR: moved the string helpers to a shared source file
    - CLEANUP: used explicit comparisons in the conditionals
    - BUG/MEDIUM: fixed several defects in the memory allocation
    - BUG/MINOR: examples: fixed three faults in the memory allocation
    - BUG/MEDIUM: moved the client handover into the thread of the worker
    - BUG/MEDIUM: released the cURL data when a worker stops
    - BUG/MINOR: fixed the build without the cURL library

2026/08/08 : 1.2.20

    Corrected the decoding of the frames received from HAProxy.  The announced
    frame length is now limited to the maximum frame size, the decoded lengths
    are checked against the space left in the frame, and an item that cannot
    be decoded aborts the whole frame.  The same corrections were also made in
    the example agent.

    The program learned the '--connection-timeout' and '--timeout' command-line
    arguments and the connection timeouts are now given in milliseconds, while
    the README got a section that describes the compatibility with HAProxy.

    The build system now supports a separate build directory and enables the
    compilation warnings.

    - BUG/MINOR: set minimum value limit for max-frame-size
    - MINOR: debug: added the mir_curl_slist_dump() function
    - CLEANUP: using the UINT64_C() macro when defining an unsigned long long value
    - MINOR: added '--connection-timeout' and '--timeout' program command-line arguments
    - CLEANUP: fixed spoa_msg_arg_hdrs() function declaration
    - BUILD/MINOR: added support for separate build directory
    - BUILD/MINOR: enable warnings and compilation errors
    - BUG/MINOR: changed connection timeouts from microseconds to milliseconds
    - BUILD/MINOR: replaced deprecated macro AC_TRY_COMPILE() (again)
    - BUG/MINOR: fixed buffer overflow on an oversized frame length
    - BUG/MINOR: fixed pointer arithmetic overflow when decoding a buffer
    - BUG/MINOR: fixed unaligned access to the frame flags
    - BUG/MINOR: examples: fixed buffer overflow and pointer arithmetic overflow
    - BUG/MINOR: fixed out-of-bounds read when decoding a 32-bit item
    - BUG/MINOR: aborted the frame decoding on a K/V item error
    - CLEANUP: checked the return value of the chdir() function
    - DOC: noted that async and fragmentation need an older HAProxy
    - DOC: added a section about the HAProxy compatibility
    - DOC: corrected the timeout defaults shown in the README
    - DOC: populated the ChangeLog

2024/04/21 : 1.2.19

    Added support for the absolute-form request target and corrected the use
    of the outgoing connection options.  The data decoder learned to decode
    whole SPOP frames.

    - CLEANUP: using the STR_ADDRSIZE() macro for working with static strings
    - MINOR: util: added possibility of decoding SPOP frames
    - BUG/MINOR: added support for absolute-form request target
    - BUG/MINOR: fixed the use of '--mirror-(interface|local-port)' program command-line arguments

2023/10/09 : 1.2.18

    The HTTP headers sent to the mirror URL can now be changed, and a program
    for decoding the data received from HAProxy was added.

    - BUG/MINOR: examples: corrected path to spoa-mirror program
    - MINOR: util: added a program for decoding data received from HAProxy via SPOP
    - CLEANUP: changing the name of the function spoa_msg_arg_hdrs()
    - MINOR: added possibility to change HTTP headers that are sent to mirror URL

2023/09/04 : 1.2.17

    The test configurations were moved into a debug subdirectory and simplified
    ones were added.  The deprecated CURLOPT_PUT option was dropped.

    - CLEANUP: examples: moved all test configurations to the 'debug' subdirectory
    - MINOR: examples: added simplified configurations for program testing
    - CLEANUP: drop CURLOPT_PUT because it is deprecated

2022/09/14 : 1.2.16

    The build system was corrected in several places, the libev library can be
    configured using pkg-config, and the call to the libev socket timer callback
    was deferred.

    - BUILD/MINOR: small corrections to the build system
    - BUILD/MINOR: replaced deprecated macro AC_TRY_COMPILE()
    - BUILD/MINOR: enabled configuration of libev library using pkg-config
    - BUILD/MINOR: remove 'typeset' from the variable definition
    - BUILD/MINOR: added libdata to PKG_CONFIG path
    - BUG/MINOR: deferred calling the libev socket timer callback function

2022/04/13 : 1.2.15

    Corrections to the debug output, among them the definition of the macro
    DBG_FUNC_END() for the non-debug mode.

    - BUG/MINOR: debug: fixed incorrectly defined 'return' statement
    - CLEANUP: debug: added a tag for the end of the function in the debug output
    - BUG/MINOR: debug: define DBG_FUNC_END() macro for non-debug mode

2022/04/12 : 1.2.14

    Better signal handling, and the debug output now shows the return values
    of all functions.

    - MINOR: better signal handling
    - fix missing put body (#23)
    - MINOR: examples: removed the deprecated global 'debug' directive
    - MINOR: debug: show return values of all functions in the debug output

2020/08/17 : 1.2.13

    Fixed the saving of the HTTP headers data in the mirror structure.

    - BUG/MINOR: fixed saving of HTTP headers data in struct mirror

2020/07/13 : 1.2.12

    The size allocation of 'struct buffer' was changed, and its initialization
    and the release of its data were improved.  The multiple execution of the
    worker_stop() function was disabled.

    - MINOR: changed 'struct buffer' size allocation
    - MINOR: improved initialization and release of 'struct buffer' data
    - BUG/MINOR: multiple execution of the function worker_stop() disabled

2020/03/19 : 1.2.11

    Fixed the calculation of the 'size' member of 'struct buffer'.

    - BUG/MINOR: fixed 'struct buffer' 'size' member calculation

2020/03/19 : 1.2.10

    The maximum debug level can be set using the value -1.

    - MINOR: allowed to set the maximum debug level using the value -1

2020/03/18 : 1.2.9

    Added a master-worker configuration file for testing the program, and the
    spoa_msg_arg_dup() function.

    - MINOR: examples: added master-worker configuration file
    - CLEANUP: added spoa_msg_arg_dup() function

2020/03/10 : 1.2.8

    Fixed the network address check.

    - BUG/MINOR: fixed network address check

2020/03/10 : 1.2.7

    The '-d' option can be used in the non-debug mode, and the buffer_grow_kv()
    function was renamed to buffer_grow_va().

    - CLEANUP: simplified frame buffer initialization
    - DOC: added some code comments in parse_url() function
    - MINOR: renamed buffer_grow_kv() function to buffer_grow_va()
    - MINOR: enabled using the '-d' option in non-debug mode

2020/02/21 : 1.2.6

    Removed the memory leaks that appeared when no HTTP requests were mirrored.

    - DOC: updated README
    - CLEANUP: removed unnecessary initialization of client structure members
    - BUG/MINOR: removed memory leaks if no HTTP requests are mirrored

2020/02/21 : 1.2.5

    Fixed the program crash in the asynchronous mode and the false positive
    warning when parsing the HTTP headers.

    - BUG/MINOR: removed false positive warning when parsing HTTP headers
    - BUG/MINOR: fixed program crash in asynchronous mode

2020/02/18 : 1.2.4

    Allowed the use of the HTTP headers with no value, and added the function
    buffer_grow_kv().

    - CLEANUP: simplified use of the debug levels in x_DBG() macros
    - CLEANUP: removed use of the DEREF_PTR() macro
    - MINOR: buffer_alloc() function definition changed
    - MINOR: added buffer_grow_kv()
    - BUG/MINOR: allowed use of HTTP headers with no value

2020/01/22 : 1.2.3

    Added the '--libev-backend' program command-line argument.

    - CLEANUP: removed the redundant lines from configure.ac
    - MINOR: added '--libev-backend' program command-line argument

2020/01/15 : 1.2.2

    The name of the worker thread is now set.

    - BUILD/MINOR: added protection against multiple __packed macro definitions
    - CLEANUP: removed duplicate debugging line
    - CLEANUP: using macro for NULL pointer checking
    - MINOR: set worker thread name

2019/09/21 : 1.2.1

    Fixed the parsing of the HAPROXY-HELLO capabilities.

    - BUILD/MINOR: enabled warning for pointer signedness difference
    - BUG/MINOR: fixed parsing of HAPROXY-HELLO capabilities

2019/07/29 : 1.2.0

    Added support for the HTTP/2 protocol.

    - MINOR: added support for HTTP/2 protocol

2019/07/29 : 1.1.0

    Added support for HTTPS and corrected the support for the query string.

    - DOC: corrected documentation related to http methods
    - BUG/MINOR: examples: corrected support for the query string
    - BUG/MINOR: changed the type of CURL_LS_* arguments
    - MINOR: added support for HTTPS

2019/07/16 : 1.0.1

    Fixed the checking of the healthcheck requests.

    - BUG/MINOR: fixed checking of healthcheck requests

2019/06/18 : 1.0.0

    The first released version.  The program is built on top of the libev and
    the cURL libraries, it processes the 'mirror' SPOE message, and it encodes
    and decodes the SPOP frames in a standardized way.

    - Initial commit
    - MINOR: deleted prefixes in error messages
    - BUG/MINOR: uninitialized variable rc
    - MINOR: added logfile status variable
    - MINOR: preserve open file descriptors in daemonize() function
    - MINOR: added '--pidfile' program command-line argument
    - MINOR: supported older versions of the cURL library
    - MINOR: reduced the minimum required version of Automake tool
    - MINOR: supported older versions of the cURL library (up from 7.32.0)
